    <item>
      <title>SAF maps Zero Trust frameworks to disciplines, roles, capabilities, and implementation — 6 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 6 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">SAF maps Zero Trust frameworks to disciplines, roles, capabilities, and implementation</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">The period centered on a substantive expansion and reorganization of Microsoft’s Security Adoption Framework guidance. New mapping guidance covers Zero Trust, the CISA Zero Trust Maturity Model, and the DoD Zero Trust Strategy, while related SAF material adds connections among business priorities, risk, responsibilities, implementation, and measurement. Two lower-impact updates refreshed titles and publication dates for MCRA and the SecOps workshop.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/products/security-adoption.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/topics/frameworks.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security adoption · Standards and frameworks</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-security-standards-and-frameworks-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">New standards-to-SAF mappings</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The new guidance maps security standards and framework objectives to SAF disciplines, roles, Microsoft security capabilities, and implementation guidance, including mappings for Zero Trust, the CISA Zero Trust Maturity Model, and the DoD Zero Trust Strategy.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/products/security-adoption.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/topics/frameworks.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security adoption · Standards and frameworks</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-microsoft-security-adoption-framework-saf-04" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">SAF now links strategy through measurement</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The SAF page now connects business priorities, risk, Zero Trust principles, security disciplines, technologies, and technical solutions, and adds guidance on shared responsibilities, implementation, measurement, and four connected framework components across hybrid, multicloud, and multiplatform environments.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/products/security-adoption.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security adoption · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-using-saf-effectively-03" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">SAF navigation shifts to goals and roles</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">“Using SAF effectively” now directs readers through tables organized around objectives and organizational roles, linking to strategy, architecture, disciplines, scenarios, technologies, workshops, and related guidance instead of the former top-down, build-up, and scenario-driven patterns.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/products/security-adoption.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security adoption · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-microsoft-cybersecurity-reference-architectures-mcra-02" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">MCRA title and publication date refreshed</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The MCRA page and heading now omit “Review,” and its publication date is shown as November 6, 2026, replacing November 2.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/products/security-operations.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.security.admin.news/assets/topics/architecture.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security operations · Strategy and deployment</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-microsoft-zero-trust-workshop-secops-05" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">SecOps workshop naming and date updated</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The Microsoft Zero Trust Workshop page now uses “SecOps” capitalization in its title and heading, and its page date changed from May 24 to November 6, 2026.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 6 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
